# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md): the subtitles of the opening movie with the European
# discs (project owner, 28.10.2026: they were missing). Only their movie/opening.sfd has a subtitle
# table in its header (CRITAGS / USRINFS, TYPE SUBTITLE: a channel per language, 3 German .. 6 Italian,
# none for English; entries with start, duration and text number); the texts are etc/movie.das (an MDT
# with six languages and a Japanese font). As their cSofdec (main.dol G4BP08 0x80161170 initApp,
# 0x8016188C initWork, 0x801615C0 draw, 0x801616E0 finishMovie, read with retail_code.py): initApp
# loads etc/movie.das as message table 2 and lays out message work 0, initWork leaves the messages on
# during the movie (DPF_MESSAGE), draw shows the text of the moment once (MesSet x 100 at the bottom,
# attribute 0x01001054) and removes it when the time leaves it, finishMovie clears and frees. Their
# newer CRI library finds the time in the playing movie; here runtime/movie_status.cpp reads the
# table from the header initApp reads anyway and compares with mwPlyGetTime. One difference: message
# table 2 is put back afterwards (theirs keeps pointing at the freed texts). Nothing changes with the
# debug build's discs. A port patch for retail data.
# Also the Japanese discs (port/docs/retail-jp-plan.md, J4: their code is the European one here).
